                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "2 Minute Video Review → https://youtu.be/pRnB2OpN-68\n\nThe original Egg Time is a free game full of crazy and hectic egg catching fun, with lots of quirky humor and surprises. The main game has chickens randomly laying eggs and you need to catch and collect as many as you can. Some eggs will enlarge or shrink your basket, make time go faster, or even spawn bombs.\nLater levels give you a freeze gun to help the pacing of eggs when there are more chickens. It’s an all around fun and silly casual game.\n\nWhich brings us to Egg Time 2. Unlike the original free game, the sequel is $7. But every single aspect of the game is more polished and improved. I think of it like the original game was the free demo, and this is the full game. It’s good as a single player casual game. But I think it really shines as a party game where everyone takes turns with others watching. For your next VR party, I recommend it.",
